{"text": "fragile", "etymologies": [{"etymologyHTML": "<p>Borrowed from Middle French <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"frm\">fragile</i>, from Latin <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"la\">fragilis</i>, formed on <i>frag-</i>, the root of <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"la\">frangere</i> (\u201cto break\u201d). Cognate with <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"en\">fraction</i>, <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"en\">fracture</i> and doublet of <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"en\">frail</i>.\n</p>", "pos": [{"pos": "Adjective", "definitions": [{"definition": "Easily broken, not sturdy; of delicate material.\n", "quote": [], "relative": {}}, {"definition": "(figuratively) Readily disrupted or destroyed.\n", "quote": [], "relative": {}}, {"definition": "(UK) Feeling weak or easily disturbed as a result of illness.", "quote": [], "relative": {}}, {"definition": "(UK) Thin-skinned or oversensitive.\n", "quote": [], "relative": {}}]}, {"pos": "Noun", "definitions": [{"definition": "Something that is fragile.", "quote": [], "relative": {}}]}]}], "pronunciation": [["UK, General Australian, Canada", "/\u02c8f\u0279\u00e6d\u0361\u0292a\u026al/"], ["US", "/\u02c8f\u0279\u00e6d\u0361\u0292\u0259l/"]]}